<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  iOS entitlements. Referenced by gen/apple/project.yml
  (targets.loca_iOS.entitlements.path), so xcodegen wires this file into the
  target; nothing else needs to change to add a key here.

  Not to be confused with src/tauri/Info.plist, which is macOS-only and says so.
  iOS declares its own strings in gen/apple/loca_iOS/Info.plist.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Loca runs the model in process on the phone, and llama.cpp loads weights
	  with mmap. File-backed pages stay evictable, so the binding constraint is
	  not the size of the GGUF but the per-app jetsam limit, and this entitlement
	  is what raises that limit on devices that support it.

	  The mmap half is a DEFAULT, not a guarantee this file can rely on. llm.mmap
	  defaults on everywhere (settings/groups/llm.ts) and inference/options.rs
	  reads it without consulting the platform, so a user who turns it off gets
	  what they asked for: resident anonymous weight pages, and a jetsam kill
	  that this entitlement raises the ceiling for but cannot prevent. That is
	  deliberate (D-178); the setting's description carries the warning.

	  Two consequences worth knowing before touching this file:

	  1. It must also be enabled on the App ID in the Apple Developer portal, or
	     it will not be in the provisioning profile and codesign FAILS the build
	     with "provisioning profile doesn't include entitlement" rather than
	     degrading. There is no macOS CI runner, so the first evidence either way
	     is a signed build on the user's machine. The portal step is item 0 in
	     M4's S0.4 session list.
	  2. It is a precondition for the S0.4 measurement rather than a result of
	     it: that session measures the jetsam ceiling WITH and WITHOUT the
	     entitlement, which it cannot do if the key is absent. The mobile fit
	     fractions in the model catalog are provisional until it has run.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
